{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-71670-r4522428","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Leong's Cashew Chicken","sourcePageId":71670,"sourceRevision":"4522428","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-10T20:48:25Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Leong's%20Cashew%20Chicken&oldid=4522428","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:14.377Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Deep fried recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using cashew","Category:Recipes using chicken breast","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"03853d8f705a526c68534983832f6da2b7e24b5c59e5758790672a09953f13b9","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chicken recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Meat Recipes|Meat Recipes]] | [[Cookbook:Midwestern cuisine|Midwestern U.S. cuisine]]\n\n'''Cashew chicken''' was invented at Leong's Tea House in Springfield, Missouri. Leong had difficulty popularizing Chinese cuisine in the area and based the dish on the popular fried foods common in the Ozarks. The dish is not truly Chinese, but rather an American dish with a \"Chinese\" theme.\n\nNote that there is also an unbreaded [[Cookbook:Cashew Chicken|cashew chicken]] recipe with softened cashews.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Chicken ===\n* 2 medium [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] breasts\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] (to taste)\n* [[Cookbook:Cashew|Cashews]], optionally [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[Cookbook:Green Onion|Green onions]], chopped\n\n=== Sauce ===\n* 1 can chicken [[Cookbook:Broth|broth]]\n* 1 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* 2 Tbsp cold water\n* 2 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 2 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Oyster sauce|oyster sauce]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Debone and cut chicken breasts into bite-sized pieces. \n#Beat eggs and mix with milk. \n#Combine flour and salt.\n#Dip breasts into egg/milk combination, then into flour.\n#[[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Deep fry]] the chicken until golden and cooked through.\n#For the sauce, heat broth in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] on low to medium heat. \n#Make a [[Cookbook:Cornstarch Slurry|cornstarch slurry]] with the cornstarch and cold water. Set aside.\n#Add oyster sauce and soy sauce to the broth. Continue heating the sauce.\n#Add the cornstarch slurry as needed to thicken the sauce until it reaches the desired consistency.  \n#Serve chicken on fried rice, cover liberally with sauce, and garnish with cashews and green onions.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken breast]]\n[[Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Deep fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Leong's Cashew Chicken","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 medium chicken breasts","sourceText":"2 medium chicken breasts","amountText":"2 medium chicken breasts","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"3 eggs","sourceText":"3 eggs","amountText":"3 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup milk","sourceText":"1 cup milk","amountText":"1 cup milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup all-purpose flour","sourceText":"1 cup all-purpose flour","amountText":"1 cup all-purpose flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Salt (to taste)","sourceText":"Salt (to taste)","amountText":"Salt (to taste)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Cashews, optionally chopped","sourceText":"Cashews, optionally chopped","amountText":"Cashews, optionally chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Green onions, chopped","sourceText":"Green onions, chopped","amountText":"Green onions, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 can chicken broth","sourceText":"1 can chicken broth","amountText":"1 can chicken broth","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 Tbsp cornstarch","sourceText":"1 Tbsp cornstarch","amountText":"1 Tbsp cornstarch","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"2 Tbsp cold water","sourceText":"2 Tbsp cold water","amountText":"2 Tbsp cold water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"2 Tbsp soy sauce","sourceText":"2 Tbsp soy sauce","amountText":"2 Tbsp soy sauce"